  "chapter": {
    "number": 140,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(141) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, I have cried to you; hear me: attend to the voice of my supplication, when I cry to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let my prayer be set forth before you as incense; the lifting up of my hands as an evening sacrifice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Set a watch, O Lord, on my mouth, and a",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 252
          },
          {
            "text": "strong door about by lips.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Incline not my heart to evil things, to",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 253
          },
          {
            "text": "employ pretexts",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 254
          },
          {
            "text": "for sins, with those who work iniquity. Let me not unite with their choice ones.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The righteous shall chasten me with mercy, and reprove me: but let not the oil of the sinner anoint my head: for yet shall my prayer also be in their",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 255
          },
          {
            "text": "pleasures.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Their mighty ones have been swallowed up near the rock: they shall hear my words, for they are sweet.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As a lump of earth is crushed upon the ground, our bones have been scattered by the mouth of the grave.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my eyes are to you, O Lord God: I have hoped in you; take not away my life.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Keep me from the snare which they have set for me, and from the stumbling blocks of them that work iniquity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sinners shall fall by their own net: I am alone until I shall escape.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 252,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Lit. a door of fortification.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 140,
          "verse": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 253,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. pretend pretences.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 140,
          "verse": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 254,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. in.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 140,
          "verse": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 255,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "q.d. lest I be injured by them.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 140,
          "verse": 5
        }
      }
    ]
